{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979573-2e-can-death-nullify-magic","id":979573,"title":"[2E] Can Death nullify magic?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-01T03:36:02-07:00","id":979573,"title":"[2E] Can Death nullify magic?","content":"In 1E Death Arcanum could 'kill' magic, regardless of used Arcanum in spell:<br /> <br /> <i>Quell the Spark (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> The mage can dispel any spell, regardless of what Arcana were used to create it \u2014 he does not need Prime 1 or any other Arcana lore. The mage must first have Mage Sight so that he can perceive the spell to be affected.</i><br /> <br /> As my partner want to makes Legacy based on resistant to others magic, could he done this with Death powers in 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-01-2016, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:19:43-07:00","id":979582,"title":"","content":"Why wouldnt Death be able to &quot;kill&quot; magic. Both endings and absence are under the purview of Death. There are many ways for that to work but starting by looking at the Prime spells for inspiration. On a metaphysical level does this also give credit to the Mysteriums view that magic is alive...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:54:28-07:00","id":979657,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/912519-can-the-death-arcanum-kill-magic#post912519\">Deja Vu...</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":".  Found it! 10-01-2016, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T11:41:05-07:00","id":979771,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <b>Char</b>, I missed this topic. So answer is more than yes, as it is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Quoting the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Looking at the flavor text of Dispel Magic, I allow Death 1 to function like Dispel, and Death 4 like Supernal Dispellation. Obviously, you need to be able to perceive the spell in question (which will be tricky without Prime), and &quot;taste&quot; of such magic might be uncomfortably close to Banishing </div> </div> </div>.<br /> <br /> So Death versions would be just Death releated rewrites of Primes spells?<br /> <br /> <i><b>Dispel Magic (Prime \u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Arcanum rating of the subject spell\u2019s caster<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills: </b>Athletics, Intimidation, Occult<br /> All Awakened magic contains the capacity to end, to allow the Fallen World\u2019s laws to reassert themselves. By Compelling these flaws in an extant spell, the mage may temporarily suppress it \u2014 or even destroy it entirely. This spell is not potent enough to dispel an archmage\u2019s spells, and only works against Awakened magic. In addition, the mage must include all Arcana involved<br /> in the casting of the subject spell at one dot. A successful casting suppresses the spell for the Duration of Dispel Magic.<br /> <b>Add Fate \u2022:</b> The mage may suppress the subject spell selectively, for a number of subjects equal to Dispel Magic\u2019s Scale factor.<br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> For one point of Mana, the effect is Lasting. If the<br /> spell\u2019s original caster is still alive and has not relinquished the<br /> spell, she knows one of her spells was destroyed.</i><br /> <br /> Should not Death Dispel just work without Arcana needed to just - it's just 'killing' magic, don't it? But then, it's basic idea for Supernal Dispellation as it is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i><b>Supernal Dispellation (Prime \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Unraveling<br /> <b>Primary Factor: </b>Potency<br /> <b>Withstand: </b>Arcanum rating of the subject spell\u2019s caster<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Athletics, Intimidation, Occult<br /> Supernal truths can never truly be unmade, but with this spell the mage may cast them back across the Abyss, effectively erasing any spell she comes across. This spell is not potent enough to dispel archmages\u2019 spells. A successful casting suppresses the spell for the Duration of Supernal Dispellation.<br /> <b>Add Fate \u2022:</b> The mage may suppress the subject spell selectively, for a number of subjects equal to the Dispel\u2019s Scale factor.<br /> <b>+2 Reach: </b>For one point of Mana, the effect is Lasting. If the spell\u2019s original caster is still alive and has not relinquished the spell, she knows one of her spells was destroyed.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-01-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T20:33:26-07:00","id":980036,"title":"","content":"I'd probably let a death ruling spell lower a spells duration, hastening it's demise. A perfecting spell should probably be able to attack a spells potency directly, &quot;damaging&quot; the spell rather than suppressing it as prime does. A making spell should be able to snuff out a spell completely as long as that spell's withstand rating is overcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T21:26:20-07:00","id":980064,"title":"","content":"Now we get to the really weird part, a Death Unmaking spell...can that &quot;resurrect&quot; an expired spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T03:29:09-07:00","id":980185,"title":"","content":"You can't target the spell to resurrect it, so I'd say no. Spells don't really leave corpses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T04:01:26-07:00","id":980187,"title":"","content":"It'd probably be possible to use Time and counter whatever shut down the spell you want to resurrect.<br /> Not entirely possible if the spell ended naturally though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T08:08:53-07:00","id":980246,"title":"",